          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field+%28physics%29"} field
            configuration of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/physical+theory"} physical theory
            of
            %em gravity
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is equivalently
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
                field, hence a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduction+of+the+structure+group"} reduction of the structure group
                of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
                along
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi O
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mi B
                        %mi GL
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{B} O(n-1,1) \to \mathbf{B}GL(n)
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+metric"} pseudo-Riemannian metric
            %li
              %p
                a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connection+on+a+bundle"} connection
                that is locally a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+algebra-valued+1-form"} Lie algebra-valued 1-form
                with values in the
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poincare+Lie+algebra"} Poincare Lie algebra
              .maruku-equation
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo ,
                      %mi Ω
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo :
                      %mi T
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %mi 𝔦𝔰𝔬
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi d
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      (E, \Omega) : T X \to \mathfrak{iso}(d-1,1)
              %p
                such that this is a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartan+connection"} Cartan connection
          %p
            (This parameterization of the gravitational field is called the
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+formulation+of+gravity"} first-order formulation of gravity
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            of the connection is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vielbein"} vielbein
            that encodes a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+metric"} pseudo-Riemannian metric
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi g
                  %mo =
                  %mi E
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g = E \cdot E
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and makes
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pseudo-Riemannian+manifold"} pseudo-Riemannian manifold
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graviton"} graviton
          %p
            The “non-propagating field”
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ω
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Omega
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+connection"} spin connection
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action+functional"} action functional
            on the space of such connection which defines the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+field+theory"} classical field theory
            of gravity is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Hilbert+action"} Einstein-Hilbert action
          %p
            More generally,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supergravity"} supergravity
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gauge+theory"} gauge theory
            over a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supermanifold"} supermanifold
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            for the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Euclidean+group"} super Poincare group
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Poincare+Lie+algebra"} super Poincare Lie algebra
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Ω
                  %mo ,
                  %mi Ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi 𝔰𝔦𝔰𝔬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (E,\Omega, \Psi) : T X \to \mathfrak{siso}(d-1,1)
          %p
            The additional
            = succeed "ic" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Ψ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Psi
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/gravitino"} gravitino
            field.
          %p
            So the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/configuration+space"} configuration space
            of gravity on some
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is essentially the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+Riemannian+metrics"} moduli space of Riemannian metrics
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
