            See also the references at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/general+relativity"} general relativity
          %h3#CovariantPhaseSpaceReferences Covariant phase space
          %p
            The (reduced)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/covariant+phase+space"} covariant phase space
            of gravity (presented for instance by its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BRST+complex"} BV-BRST complex
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Romeo+Brunetti"}> Romeo Brunetti
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Fredenhagen"} Klaus Fredenhagen
              %em Towards a Background Independent Formulation of Perturbative Quantum Gravity
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/0603079"}> arXiv:gr-qc/0603079
              )
          %p which is surveyed in
          %ul
            %li
              Katarzyna Rejzner,
              %em The BV formalism applied to classical gravity
              (
              %a{:href => "http://rejzner.com/talks/Karlsruhe2011.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %p
            Careful discussion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/observables"} observables
            in gravity is in
          %ul
            %li#Khavkine14
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Igor+Khavkine"}> Igor Khavkine
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Local and gauge invariant observables in gravity
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.science.unitn.it/~moretti/convegno/convegno.html"} Operator and Geometric Analysis on Quantum Theory
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1503.03754"} arXiv:1503.03754
          %p
            Further discussion of the phase space of gravity in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/first-order+formulation+of+gravity"} first-order formulation
            via
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BV-BFV+formalism"} BV-BFV formalism
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michele+Schiavina"}> Michele Schiavina
                ,
                %em BV-BFV approach to general relativity
                (2015) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "http://user.math.uzh.ch/cattaneo/schiavina.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Schiavina-Relativity.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#CattaneoSchiavina15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Cattaneo"}> Alberto Cattaneo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michele+Schiavina"} Michele Schiavina
                = succeed "," do
                  %em BV-BFV approach to General Relativity, Einstein-Hilbert action
                %strong 57
                023515 (2016) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1509.05762"}> arXiv:1509.05762
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1063/1.4941410"} doi:10.1063/1.4941410
            %li#CattaneoSchiavina17a
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Cattaneo"}> Alberto Cattaneo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michele+Schiavina"} Michele Schiavina
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The reduced phase space of Palatini-Cartan-Holst theory
                %strong 20
                (2019) 445 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.05351"}> arXiv:1707.05351
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/s00023-018-0733-z"} doi:10.1007/s00023-018-0733-z
            %li#CattaneoSchiavina17b
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+Cattaneo"}> Alberto Cattaneo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michele+Schiavina"} Michele Schiavina
                = succeed "," do
                  %em BV-BFV approach to General Relativity: Palatini-Cartan-Holst action
                %strong 23
                (2019) 1801-1835 &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1707.06328"}> arXiv:1707.06328
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.4310/ATMP.2019.v23.n8.a3"} doi:10.4310/ATMP.2019.v23.n8.a3
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+S.+Cattaneo"}> Alberto S. Cattaneo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Phase space for gravity with boundaries
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Encyclopedia+of+Mathematical+Physics+2nd+ed"} Encyclopedia of Mathematical Physics 2nd ed
                (2023) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2307.04666"}> arXiv:2307.04666
                \&amp;rbrack;
              %blockquote
                %p
                  (following
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "phase+space#KijowskiTulczyjew05"} Kijowski &amp; Tulczyjew (2005)
          %p Discussion of flux-observables:
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alberto+S.+Cattaneo"}> Alberto S. Cattaneo
              , Alejandro Perez,
              = succeed "," do
                %em A note on the Poisson bracket of 2d smeared fluxes in loop quantum gravity
              %strong 34
              (2017) 107001 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1611.08394"}> arXiv:1611.08394
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1361-6382/aa69b4"} doi:10.1088/1361-6382/aa69b4
          %h3#nonrenormalizability Non-renormalizability
          %p
            The result that gravity is not
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/renormalizable+interaction"} renormalizable
            is due to:
          %ul
            %li#tHooftVelrman74
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gerard+%27t+Hooft"}> Gerard 't Hooft
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Martinus+Veltman"} Martinus Veltman
              = succeed "," do
                %em One loop divergencies in the theory of gravitation
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "AIHPA_1974__20_1_69_0"} numdam:AIHPA_1974__20_1_69_0
          %p Review:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zvi+Bern"}> Zvi Bern
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Perturbative quantum gravity and its relation to gauge theory
                %a{:href => "www.livingreviews.org/Articles/Volume5/2002-5bern"} www.livingreviews.org/Articles/Volume5/2002-5bern
            %li
              %p
                Assaf Shomer,
                %em A pedagogical explanation for the non-renormalizability of gravity
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0709.3555"}> arXiv:0709.3555
                )
          %h3#induced_gravity Induced gravity
          %ul
            %li
              Matt Visser:
              = succeed "," do
                %em Sakharov’s induced gravity: a modern perspective
              %strong 17
              (2002) 977-992 &amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/gr-qc/0204062"}> arXiv:gr-qc/0204062
              ,
              = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/S0217732302006886"} doi:10.1142/S0217732302006886
